-- title:
--   Drinfeld's deformation ring has Krull dimension at least two
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and let $O^{nr}$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring and a $\mathbb{Z}_q$-algebra, such that the ideal generated by the image of $q$ is maximal and $O^{nr}$ is complete for the adic topology it defines, and whose residue field is algebraically closed. Let $\iota : W(\mathbb{F}_{q^2}) \to O^{nr}$ be a ring homomorphism and let $X_0$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over the residue field of $O^{nr}$ for the reduction of $\iota$ — that is, a commutative $2$-dimensional formal group law $F$ together with series $\mathrm{act}(a)$ ($a \in W(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})$) and $\varpi$, all law endomorphisms of $F$, with $\mathrm{act}$ additive and multiplicative, $\varpi \circ \varpi = \mathrm{act}(q)$ and $\varpi \circ \mathrm{act}(a) = \mathrm{act}(\sigma a) \circ \varpi$ for the Witt-vector Frobenius $\sigma$ — which is special, in that the Lie summands $\mathrm{lieZero}$ and $\mathrm{lieOne}$ attached to $\iota$ are complementary and each invertible, and of height $4$, in that $\mathrm{act}(q)$ has kernel of degree $q^4$. Let $R$ be a noetherian local $O^{nr}$-algebra, complete for its maximal ideal, equipped with $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ to the residue field of $O^{nr}$ restricting to the residue map on $O^{nr}$, a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X_u$ over $R$, and an isomorphism $w_u$ from the base change of $X_u$ along $\mathrm{res}_R$ to $X_0$. Assume the pro-representability hypothesis: for every artinian local $O^{nr}$-algebra $A$ with surjective residue-compatible $\mathrm{res}_A : A \to k$, every special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X$ over $A$ of height $4$ (relative to $\iota$ composed with $O^{nr} \to A$) and every isomorphism $w$ from the base change of $X$ along $\mathrm{res}_A$ to $X_0$, there is a unique $O^{nr}$-algebra homomorphism $\chi : R \to A$ with $\mathrm{res}_A \circ \chi = \mathrm{res}_R$ admitting an isomorphism $v$ from the base change of $X_u$ along $\chi$ to $X$ with $w \circ (v \otimes \mathrm{res}_A)$ given by the same series as $w_u$. Then $\dim R \ge 2$.
--
--   This is the lower bound in Drinfeld's determination of the universal deformation ring of a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module of height $4$ over an algebraically closed field, which is either $O^{nr}[[t]]$ or $O^{nr}[[u,v]]/(uv-q)$; the corresponding upper bound is obtained from tangent-space computations, and the two together give the dichotomy asserted in [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.isRegularLocalRing_and_nonempty_algEquiv_powerSeries_or_uvCrossingModel_of_isProrepresentedBy_deformations`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.isRegularLocalRing_and_nonempty_algEquiv_powerSeries_or_uvCrossingModel_of_isProrepresentedBy_deformations), which cites this result.
